! CASSCF def2-SVP TightSCF MOREAD NoIter
# Gate-2 reference for Cr(acac)3.
#
# Unlike TiCl3, the SA-CASSCF(3,5) for this system is run externally and
# arrives as cracac-cas35.gbw. This job does NOT re-optimize it: it reads
# those orbitals back (MOREAD + NoIter) and re-diagonalizes the full d^3
# manifold in them -- 10 quartets + 40 doublets -- so that step 02 has
# per-root ORCA energies to check the MOKIT transfer against.
#
# Why maxiter 1 and not 0: `maxiter 0` makes ORCA 6 skip the CI solve
# entirely, print "ROOT 0: E= 0.0000000000" and then die with an I/O
# error. `maxiter 1` runs the INITIAL CI STATE CHECK -- a CASCI in exactly
# the input orbitals -- and reports DE = 0.000000e+00, so the printed
# CAS-SCF STATES tables are the CASCI roots of the imported orbitals. That
# is a STRONGER gate than comparing a single state-averaged energy, and it
# does not require knowing what weights the original SA-CASSCF used.
#
# Measured: the orbital gradient at these orbitals under a 10-quartet +
# 40-doublet equal-block average is ||g|| = 3.1e-04 (Max 6.6e-05), i.e.
# essentially stationary; and PySCF CASCI reproduces all 50 roots to
# 2.8e-08 Ha.
#
# Serial by design -- this build of ORCA has no mpirun. Add `%pal nprocs N
# end` on a cluster node. Runtime: ~2 min on 1 core.

%moinp "cracac-cas35.gbw"
%maxcore 3000
%casscf
  nel     3
  norb    5
  mult    4,2
  nroots  10,40
  maxiter 1
end

* xyzfile 0 4 cracac-r2scan3c-opt1.xyz
